<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Value after appreciation</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(ix=1)"]]A plot in Kitengela[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=2)"]]An apartment in Nakuru[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=3)"]]A commercial plot in Eldoret[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=4)"]]A shamba in Kiambu[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=5)"]]A house in Kisumu[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=6)"]]A plot in Machakos[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=7)"]]A hotel plot in Malindi[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=8)"]]A plot in Thika[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=9)"]]A house in Nyeri[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=10)"]]A plot in Naivasha[[/if]] was bought for Ksh \({@ksh(P)@}\). Its value appreciates at \({@dd(r)@}\%\) a year.</p><p>(a) Find its value after \({@n@}\) years, to the nearest shilling.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the appreciation over the \({@n@}\) years.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The value is multiplied by the same number, \(1 + \frac{ {@dd(r)@} }{100} = {@dd(mult)@}\), every year.</p><p>(a) \(V = {@ksh(P)@} \times {@dd(mult)@}^{ {@n@} } = {@ksh(V)@}\), so the value is Ksh \({@ksh(floor(V+1/2))@}\) to the nearest shilling.</p><p>(b) Appreciation \(= V - P = {@ksh(V)@} - {@ksh(P)@} = {@ksh(G)@}\)[[if test="not(integerp(G))"]], about Ksh \({@ksh(floor(G+1/2))@}\)[[/if]].</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: growth by a fixed percentage, in land contexts. [P, r, n]. Source: adapted from SMP GCSE Higher book 2, chapter 24, A3 and A4. */
L: [[1500000,9,4],[850000,12,4],[3200000,15/2,5],[640000,14,2],[2250000,8,5],[1180000,11,3],[4600000,13/2,4],[720000,14,3],[2900000,10,5],[960000,25/2,2]];
E: L[ix];
P: E[1]; r: E[2]; n: E[3];
mult: 1+r/100;
V: P*mult^n;
G: V-P;
/* diagnostics */
Vs: P*(1+r*n/100);
Vd: P*(1-r/100)^n;
Vm: P*mult^(n-1);
Gs: P*r*n/100;
G1: P*r/100;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
