  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Commercial Arithmetic III: value after appreciation</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 2.4 (c): Find the value of land or a house after several years of appreciation at a fixed yearly rate, and the appreciation.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 24 (Exponential growth and decay), Section A, questions A3 and A4 of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Higher 2 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2007: growth by a fixed percentage each year; land and houses in Kenyan towns, new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
